Article 15. Response to and remediation of cyber security incidents
for information systems of national security importance
1. Response to and remediation of cyber security incidents for information systems of
national security importance include:
a/ Detecting and identifying cyber security incidents;
b/ Protecting scenes and collecting evidence;
c/ Blocking or limiting the scope of, and minimizing damage caused by, cyber
security incidents;
d/ Identifying targets in need and scope of response;
dd/ Verifying, analyzing,

dd/ Verifying, analyzing, assessing and classifying cyber security incidents;
e/ Implementing cyber security incident response and remediation plans;
f/ Identifying causes and sources of incidents;
g/ Investigating and handling in accordance with law.
2. Managers of information systems of national security importance shall prepare cyber
security incident response and remediation plans for these information systems; implement
the plans when cyber security incidents occur and promptly report them to a competent
professional cyber security protection force.

